Package: sandtablR
Title: Mass-Casualty Incident Simulation and Machine Learning Workbench
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("R.", "Heller", email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742")),
    person("Gerhard", "Achatz", role = "aut"))
Description: A generic framework for mass-casualty incident tabletop
    exercise simulation, decision-path analysis and machine learning. The
    package provides a discrete-event patient-flow engine, a tidy data model
    for scenarios, patient cards and decision paths, and synthetic cohort
    generation. It supports supervised triage and therapy-concept
    classification with interpretable and black-box models, sequence analysis
    of participant decision paths and a model-agnostic explainability layer.
    An interactive 'shiny' workbench ties the pieces together for scenario
    building, simulation, model training, comparison and visualisation.
